[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614968111","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2614968111","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2614968111,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b3T8v","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T06:53:13Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T06:53:13Z","body":"> I think it would be nice to have this pop-up display automatically when a project is first opened in 4.4 from a previous version, although I'm not sure yet how easy that would be to do. I hope to look more into that in the coming days, but in the meantime the tool is accessible through the menu bar as described previously.\r\n\r\nTry to check [`ProjectManager::_open_selected_projects_check_warnings()`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e5498020b6250d9284efcdcf0f85f39d48d8548f/editor/project_manager.cpp#L526).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614968111/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615873006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2615873006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2615873006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b6w3u","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T14:13:21Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T14:13:21Z","body":"I wonder... We have Surface Upgrade Tool and now the UID Upgrade, but they both serve more or less the same task - open and re-save files. The problem is that they don't handle all files, so if we want to upgrade something else in the future, we will need another upgrade tool.\r\n\r\nThe script I posted in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11639#issuecomment-2615863255 handles pretty much all relevant files in a future-proof way, and it's only 27 lines. Maybe we should just have a single universal \"upgrade tool\" that user is supposed to run manually when opening in a new version? If it handles every resource there won't be any need for new tools, unless for something very specific that involves more than load and save.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615873006/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615945451","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2615945451","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2615945451,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b7Cjr","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T14:41:18Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T14:43:24Z","body":"I wonder if we can add a third button in the dialog that opens https://godotengine.org/article/uid-changes-coming-to-godot-4-4/ in a web browser. It would be helpful to give more context to users as to why the change was done, especially if they don't follow changelogs.\r\n\r\nAt the very least, the dialog's text should state that the new `.uid` files should be added to version control.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615945451/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616483375","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2616483375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2616483375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b9F4v","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T17:41:06Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T17:41:06Z","body":"> Try to check [`ProjectManager::_open_selected_projects_check_warnings()`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e5498020b6250d9284efcdcf0f85f39d48d8548f/editor/project_manager.cpp#L526).\r\n\r\nThanks, I'll give that a look soon!\r\n\r\n\r\n> The script I posted in [godotengine/godot-proposals#11639 (comment)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11639#issuecomment-2615863255) handles pretty much all relevant files in a future-proof way, and it's only 27 lines. Maybe we should just have a single universal \"upgrade tool\" that user is supposed to run manually when opening in a new version? If it handles every resource there won't be any need for new tools, unless for something very specific that involves more than load and save.\r\n\r\nI like this idea! As stated previously, this PR is basically just an adaptation of the existing surface tool code anyways, so there's a lot of code there that's at best duplicate-adjacent. \r\n\r\nI'm not sure how \"hard\" the 4.4 feature freeze is; my hope was that, because the UID change introduces such a big friction point for updating and keeping clean version control, this tool could be added to 4.4 so that people could use it to upgrade their projects as soon as 4.4 becomes available. In that case, I'd be a bit nervous about expanding the scope of this PR to act as a more general project updater, since there'd be more possibility of bugs cropping up.\r\n\r\nHowever, if the feature freeze wouldn't allow this to be included until 4.4.1 (or 4.5) then we'd have a lot more time to get it polished and ready for its release. In the meantime, your script and instructions on how to run it could be included in the blog posts about 4.4's release.\r\n\r\n> I wonder if we can add a third button in the dialog that opens https://godotengine.org/article/uid-changes-coming-to-godot-4-4/ in a web browser. It would be helpful to give more context to users as to why the change was done, especially if they don't follow changelogs.\r\n> \r\n> At the very least, the dialog's text should state that the new `.uid` files should be added to version control.\r\n\r\nI've added a bit of text stating the user should add `.uid` files. As for the third button, I see that `AcceptDialog` does have a method to add custom buttons to it, so I can look into adding a \"learn more\" button to the dialog.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2616483375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617131825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2617131825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2617131825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b_kMx","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T23:32:39Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T23:32:39Z","body":"Well for 4.4 the current solution makes sense. We could refactor it in the future. The universal tool would replace existing ones.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617131825/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617540770","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2617540770","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2617540770,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cBICi","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T02:01:17Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T04:28:52Z","body":"I've added a \"Learn more\" button to the dialog box that opens the blog post about UIDs. It appears the current API for AcceptDialog only allows for it to be placed either to the left or to the right of all the buttons, so for now I have it on the right.\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2025-01-27 at 17 55 59@2x](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1fc62bc9-ed32-497d-bc64-0fed5fb6dd9e)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI looked at `_open_selected_projects_check_warnings` and it doesn't sound to me like it would quite fit what we need, since it runs in the project manager before the main editor is open. ~~I also gave a shot at reading through the core/editor code to find where we could detect a 4.3 (or lower) project had been opened in 4.4, but nothing stuck out to me. I may give it another shot tomorrow, but if it looks like it's going to get too complex adding this check in, we may just want to tell people to find the option in the Tools menu.~~\r\n\r\nI looked into it a bit further and found a spot that looks promising! Working on it now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617540770/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617839661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2617839661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2617839661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cCRAt","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T04:50:32Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T04:50:32Z","body":"The tool window is now displayed automatically when the editor is started with a project on 4.3 or less!\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/230c6a1f-5b32-4528-ab5b-536c26f17eb4\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617839661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619132862","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2619132862","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2619132862,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cHMu-","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T14:17:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T14:17:59Z","body":"The dialog appears too early and progress dialog will overlay it:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82187f26-60c9-4e7a-8975-beca88d2be05)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619132862/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619628590","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2619628590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2619628590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cJFwu","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T17:24:12Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T17:24:12Z","body":"Thanks for pointing this out! I was feeling like popping it up at the end of the EditorNode constructor wasn't *quite* right, but I wasn't sure where else to put it...\r\n\r\nWith your screenshot, it occurred to me that the check could be run immediately after `_load_editor_layout` when doing the first scan. I'll give that a try soon!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619628590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2620753723","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102071#issuecomment-2620753723","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102071","id":2620753723,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cNYc7","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T05:32:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-29T05:32:08Z","body":"I've changed the order of detecting a 4.3 project and displaying the popup now so that it appears after the progress dialog:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/98d1bebb-2349-4839-bf6c-14f1e9a7be78\r\n\r\n- When the EditorNode receives the `READY` notification, it checks the project's version number *before* performing an initial save of the project settings. If it detects the project is from 4.3 or before, it activates a flag variable.\r\n- Later, when the `_sources_changed` method is evaluated, it checks that flag variable. If the flag is true, it sets it back to false (to avoid re-triggering the popup in the future) and 